# Leg-hold trap (#561, D128), native 32x16, bottom row on the floor line. DISGUISED (D71): a leg-hold lies on the ground under leaves.
# open (at rest): a 5 px mound of leaf litter, columns 4-27 (the lethal span, x + 4 to x + 28), over the flat jaws; the always-drawn cue is two bone tooth tips, a sinew wrap at
# each end of the litter and a peg with its cord. rattle1/rattle2 (the D7 warning, 0.1 s each): the leaves shiver. snap: the leaves burst and the
# jaws spring up to 14 px. shut: the folded jaws, harmless. rearm: the leaves settle back and the cue (tips, wraps, peg and cord) stays.
size 32 16
color k 0b0814
color b 4a2e1c
color B 8a5a30
